[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_mgaiq")
dialogue_id = "debate_magic_science"
record_title = "Debate Speech: Magic Rituals"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: Back when the priests among our ancestors practiced magical rituals, they settled a shard we now call The Fox Spirits Domain.
historian: Even though the Scribes of the past called these foxes evil spirits, the priests of this shard chose to study them instead of taking immediate action.
historian: By putting away their holy wards and opening their eyes, they learned to see the world as it is.
historian: Today they learn medicine by watching what herbs sick monkeys chew on, and protect their crops by breeding the right kind of beetles.
historian: Our history is full of stories of looking at things we do not understand and calling them divine mysteries.
historian: We let these mysteries inspire elaborate rituals, in an effort to tame the unknown.
historian: But these rituals are just the first, clumsy steps toward understanding the world.
historian: If we turn the Scribe's holy mandates into absolute laws, we will freeze our minds in the present and stop learning.
historian: We must leave our people free to put down the sacred texts and look at reality not as it ought to be, but as it really is."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
